{"id": "e9097fb3-5c91-4afd-87f2-bce03bbac718", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a scoped audit across SageMaker notebooks and domains for internet exposure and encryption at rest — a token-heavy survey best handed to a background sub-agent rather than me digging through it directly. I'll tell the user the plan, then delegate, maybe checking associations first so the subagent knows which accounts to cover.

I'll give it a structured, read-only prompt: check notebook instances for direct internet access, root access, KMS keys, subnets and security groups, plus domains for network access type, EFS encryption, and associated subnets/security groups, across all relevant regions and accounts. I'll preload the topology-discovery skill and restrict it to use_aws only.

"}]}

{"id": "ef6f920c-4e1c-4b74-be04-5cb99be2f8a3", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit your SageMaker notebook instances and domains across the associated accounts and regions. For each one I'll check internet exposure (direct internet access, public vs VPC-only networking, security groups) and encryption at rest (KMS keys on volumes and EFS). Surveying every region means a lot of intermediate data, so I'll run it in the background and summarize the findings.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_DYnobOnu5MKFGHQatqDuAK", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-exposure-encryption-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only security audit of Amazon SageMaker notebook instances and SageMaker domains (Studio) for (a) internet exposure and (b) encryption at rest.",
  "context": "User wants a posture audit across all AWS accounts associated with this agent space (use list_associations to find them; the agent space's own account is 012345678901_1, home region us-east-1) and across all regions where SageMaker is available/used. Do NOT make any mutating calls. Enumerate every region (e.g., via ec2 describe_regions or account-enabled regions) and handle pagination; skip regions that error with access/opt-in issues and note them.",
  "resources": ["sagemaker list_notebook_instances / describe_notebook_instance", "sagemaker list_domains / describe_domain", "sagemaker list_user_profiles / list_spaces (only if needed for domain-level encryption/exposure)", "ec2 describe_subnets / describe_security_groups / describe_route_tables (to determine whether VPC subnets have an IGW route / public IPs and whether SGs allow 0.0.0.0/0 inbound)", "kms describe_key / list_aliases (to distinguish AWS-managed vs customer-managed keys)"],
  "timeframe": "Current state (point-in-time)",
  "criteria": "Notebook instances: flag DirectInternetAccess=Enabled; flag RootAccess=Enabled; flag instances not in a VPC (no SubnetId); flag security groups with inbound 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0; report KmsKeyId (missing = no CMK on the ML storage volume; note whether AWS-managed vs customer-managed); report NotebookInstanceStatus. Domains: flag AppNetworkAccessType=PublicInternetOnly (vs VpcOnly); report SubnetIds, security groups (DomainSettings / DefaultUserSettings.SecurityGroups) and whether subnets are public (route to igw / MapPublicIpOnLaunch); report KmsKeyId (EFS home volume encryption) and any domain-level encryption for the managed storage; note whether the domain uses a CMK vs AWS-managed key; note any domain-level settings relevant to internet exposure (e.g., presigned URL / DefaultUserSettings sharing settings, RStudio, JupyterLab). Return: (1) counts of resources audited per account/region, (2) a concise findings table of ONLY non-compliant or notable resources with resource name, account, region, finding, and severity (High/Medium/Low), (3) list of compliant resources summarized as counts, (4) any regions/accounts you could not access, (5) brief remediation guidance per finding type (note that DirectInternetAccess and KmsKeyId on existing notebook instances cannot be changed in place and require recreating the instance; domain KmsKeyId/AppNetworkAccessType also generally require recreation/migration - verify with documentation if unsure). Keep the report concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker notebooks and domains for exposure and encryption"}], "created_at": null}

